From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:15:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: read MCP stdin byte by byte on a plain thread

Problem: on AROS a read from a PIPE: handler returns only when the whole
  requested length has arrived or the writer closed it (rust-aros process
  evidence, 2026-10-15). Tokio's stdin, over std's 8 KiB buffer, asks for
  kilobytes, so a client's short MCP request would stay unread until the
  client closed its side.
Rationale: serve_stdio on AROS takes its input from a thread that reads
  descriptor 0 one byte per call (bypassing std's buffer) and
  passes complete lines (at most 64 KiB at a time) to an AsyncRead; output
  stays Tokio's stdout. The thread ends at end of input, which is how a
  stdio MCP session ends, so it never outlives the session it serves.
  serve_io, rmcp, the tools and the protocol are unchanged. Descriptor 0
  is taken as a File by the new photocraft-aros-stdin crate (automation
  forbids unsafe code); duplicating it fails with EINVAL on this ABIv11
  C library (no F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC), seen on pool v11-2.
Scope: cfg(target_os = "aros") in crates/automation server transport;
  new crate crates/aros-stdin.
Upstream-status: local-only.
Prerequisites: 0007.
Verification: the guest MCP acceptance run (tests/mcp-client).
Removal: when stdin reads on AROS return what is available.
